	| Comment     | Request Comment  |
	| Attachments | Document_1.txt   |

Scenario: View Closed Request
	Closed requests should only contain certain options.

	Given I create a user with the following values
	| Name             | Zendesk Enduser1                    |
	| Tags             | osb_customer,osb_kb                 |
	| Password         | zendeskqauser                       |
	| Role             | End-user                            |
	| Access           | Organization                        |
	| Email            | zendesk.enduser1@zendesk.com.broken |
	| Phone Number     | +1 (555) 555-5555                   |
	| Organization     | Frontend Org Name 1                 |
	| Language         | English                             |
	| Time Zone        | Pacific Time (US & Canada)          |
	| External ID      | Enduser1                            |
	And I create a user with the following values
	| Name             | Zendesk Endagent1                    |
	| Password         | zendeskqauser                        |
	| Role             | Agent                                |
	| Email            | zendesk.endagent1@liferay.com.broken |
	| Phone Number     | +1 (555) 555-5555                    |
	| Language         | English                              |
	| Time Zone        | Pacific Time (US & Canada)           |
	| External ID      | Endagent1                            |
	And I assign the user with the email address "zendesk.endagent1@liferay.com.broken" to the group "Provisioning - US"
	And I create a request as a user with the email address "zendesk.enduser1@zendesk.com.broken" with the following values
	| Product                  | prd_liferay_dxp_7_3                              |
	| Component                | activation_key_project_administration            |
	| System Status            | production_functioning_with_limited_capabilities |
	| Subject                  | Request Subject                                  |
	| Description              | Request Description                              |
	| Organization External ID | FrontendOrg1                                     |
	And I assign the ticket with the ID "${staticRequestIdList}" to a user with the email address "zendesk.endagent1@liferay.com.broken"
	And I change the status and sub-status of the ticket with the ID "${staticRequestIdList}" to "solved" and "completed" respectively
	And I assign a ticket with the ID "${staticRequestIdList}" with the following tags
	| auto_closed |
	When I log into zendesk as "zendesk.enduser1@zendesk.com.broken" with password "zendeskqauser"
	And I go to My activities
	And I click on the request with the subject "Request Subject" in the index
	Then I should be able to view a request with the following details
	| Subject       | Request Subject                                    |
	| Status        | SOLVED                                             |
	| Requester     | Zendesk Enduser1                                   |
	| Assigned to   | Zendesk Endagent1                                  |
	| Priority      | Normal                                             |
	| Product       | Liferay DXP > 7.3                                  |
	| Sub-Status    | Completed                                          |
	| Component     | Activation Key & Project Administration            |
	| System Status | Production > Functioning with limited capabilities |
	And I should not see the request comment field
	And I should see the closed comment message
	And I should not see the large attachment link

Scenario: Create Follow Up
	End users should be able to create a follow up on a closed ticket.

	Given I create a user with the following values
	| Name             | Zendesk Enduser1                    |
	| Tags             | osb_customer,osb_kb                 |
	| Password         | zendeskqauser                       |
	| Role             | End-user                            |
	| Access           | Organization                        |
	| Email            | zendesk.enduser1@zendesk.com.broken |
	| Phone Number     | +1 (555) 555-5555                   |
	| Organization     | Frontend Org Name 1                 |
	| Language         | English                             |
	| Time Zone        | Pacific Time (US & Canada)          |
	| External ID      | Enduser1                            |
	And I create a user with the following values
	| Name             | Zendesk Endagent1                    |
	| Password         | zendeskqauser                        |
	| Role             | Agent                                |
	| Email            | zendesk.endagent1@liferay.com.broken |
	| Phone Number     | +1 (555) 555-5555                    |
	| Language         | English                              |
	| Time Zone        | Pacific Time (US & Canada)           |
	| External ID      | Endagent1                            |
	And I assign the user with the email address "zendesk.endagent1@liferay.com.broken" to the group "Provisioning - US"
	And I create a request as a user with the email address "zendesk.enduser1@zendesk.com.broken" with the following values
	| Product                  | prd_liferay_dxp_7_3                              |
	| Component                | activation_key_project_administration            |
	| System Status            | production_functioning_with_limited_capabilities |
	| Subject                  | Request Subject                                  |
	| Description              | Request Description                              |
	| Organization External ID | FrontendOrg1                                     |
	And I assign the ticket with the ID "${staticRequestIdList}" to a user with the email address "zendesk.endagent1@liferay.com.broken"
	And I change the status and sub-status of the ticket with the ID "${staticRequestIdList}" to "solved" and "completed" respectively
	And I assign a ticket with the ID "${staticRequestIdList}" with the following tags
	| auto_closed |
	When I log into zendesk as "zendesk.enduser1@zendesk.com.broken" with password "zendeskqauser"
	And I go to My activities
	And I click on the request with the subject "Request Subject" in the index
	And I create a follow-up request
	Then I should be able to view a request with the following details
	| Subject       | Re: Request Subject                                |
	| Status        | OPEN                                               |
	| Requester     | Zendesk Enduser1                                   |
	| Priority      | Normal                                             |
	| Product       | Liferay DXP > 7.3                                  |
	| Sub-Status    | Completed                                          |
	| Component     | Activation Key & Project Administration            |
	| System Status | Production > Functioning with limited capabilities |
	And I should see the request comment field
	And I should not see the closed comment message
	And I should be able to view a request comment containing the text "This is a follow-up to your previous request" with the following details
	| Author          | Zendesk Enduser1                             |
	| Partial Comment | This is a follow-up to your previous request |
	| Partial Comment | "Request Subject"                            |

