	When I click the option "Back"
	And I click the option "Non-Production"
	Then I should see the following options
	| Completely shutdown                   |
	| Severely impacted or inoperable       |
	| Unstable with periodic interruptions  |
	| Functioning with limited capabilities |
	| Fully functional with observed errors |
	When I click the option "Back"
	And I click the option "-"
	Then I should see the Subject text field
	And I should see the Description text field

Scenario: View large file warnings
	End users should be able to view large file warnings on the request submit form and comment submit form.

	Given I create a user with the following values
	| Name             | Zendesk Enduser1                    |
	| Tags             | osb_customer,osb_kb                 |
	| Password         | zendeskqauser                       |
	| Role             | End-user                            |
	| Access           | Organization                        |
	| Email            | zendesk.enduser1@zendesk.com.broken |
	| Phone Number     | +1 (555) 555-5555                   |
	| Organization     | Frontend Org Name 1                 |
	| Language         | English                             |
	| Time Zone        | Pacific Time (US & Canada)          |
	| External ID      | Enduser1                            |
	When I log into zendesk as "zendesk.enduser1@zendesk.com.broken" with password "zendeskqauser"
	And I go to the Submit a ticket form
	Then I should be able to view the large file attachment warning on the request add page
	When I create a request as a user with the email address "zendesk.enduser1@zendesk.com.broken" with the following values
	| Product                  | prd_liferay_dxp_7_3                              |
	| Component                | activation_key_project_administration            |
	| System Status            | production_functioning_with_limited_capabilities |
	| Subject                  | Request Subject                                  |
	| Description              | Request Description                              |
	| Organization External ID | FrontendOrg1                                     |
	And I go to My activities
	And I click on the request with the subject "Request Subject" in the index
	Then I should be able to view the large file attachment warning on the request comment form